<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bir Singh Deo Tomar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bir Singh Deo, also called Virasimha, was a Tomara <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> chief who founded the Tomara dynasty of Gwalior in the late 14th century. Serving the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> as its power weakened in the 1390s, he took control of the great hill fort of Gwalior and ruled it as an independent prince. His successors, among them the builder king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/man-singh-tomar">Man Singh Tomar</a>, held Gwalior until it fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodi-dynasty">Lodi</a> sultans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> in the early 16th century.</p></div>
